# Git Sync Service Environment Variables

# ENCRYPTION_KEY is required for credential encryption (AES-256-GCM).
# This key is used to encrypt/decrypt access tokens stored in the database.
# - Minimum length: 1 byte (will be hashed to 32 bytes via SHA-256)
# - Recommended: Use a strong passphrase of at least 32 characters
# - Keys of exactly 32 bytes are used directly as AES-256 keys
# - Keys of other lengths are hashed with SHA-256 to derive a 32-byte key
#
# Generate a secure key:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Or use a passphrase:
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY="my-secret-passphrase-at-least-32-chars"
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
